; A fixed BOOL literal in MEMBER position (`[v: true]` / `{k: false}`) is SUPPORTED: the
; fixed-value deserialize arm has a `FixedValue::Bool` case that reads `raw.bool()?`, compares it
; against the literal, and raises `FixedValueMismatch { found: Key::Bool, expected: Key::Bool }`
; on a mismatch (mirroring the Uint/Text arms; serialize already wrote `Special::Bool`). This
; fixture is the regression pin that the shape GENERATES rather than panicking the deserialize
; catch-all; tests/corpus/fixed_bool_member.cddl additionally round-trips the mandatory array/map
; placements and the tag-wrapped members (OPTIONAL fixed-value placements stay a pre-existing
; generation-failure class — see cddl-matrix/roadmap.toml § findings).
; Distinct from neighboring shapes that stay REJECTED, all of them gracefully: top-level
; `foo = true` (tests/matrix_reject/prelude.true.cddl), a fixed value under a count-permitting
; occurrence `[* true]` (tests/robustness/fixed_value_occurrence.cddl) and its table-VALUE sibling
; (tests/robustness/fixed_table_value.cddl), a bool MAP KEY `{ true => uint }` (MapKeyKind
; rejection), and a tagged prelude constant `#6.11(true)`
; (tests/robustness/tagged_prelude_constant.cddl). What separates this fixture's shape from all of
; them is CARDINALITY: exactly one occurrence needs no per-repetition storage, so the fixed member
; can be checked on the wire and stored nowhere. Matrix rows `contain.array-element.prelude.true`,
; `contain.map-value.prelude.false`, `contain.array-element.type2.tag.fixed_null`, and
; `contain.array-element.type2.tag.fixed_bool` carry the mandatory member containment verdicts; this
; hand fixture remains the support/reject boundary for neighboring shapes.
arr = [v: true, x: uint]
